> **NexaTech Solutions Raises $85 Million in Series C Funding to Accelerate Growth and Innovation in AI-Powered Business Intelligence**
> 
> **AUSTIN, TX – September 15, 2025** – NexaTech Solutions Inc., a leader in AI-powered business intelligence and data analytics, today announced that it has closed an $85 million Series C funding round. The round was led by Summit Peak Investments, with participation from existing investors TechGrowth Capital and Global Ventures Group.
> 
> This latest round of funding will be used to accelerate NexaTech’s global expansion, scale its sales and marketing efforts, and further invest in the development of its innovative AI-driven analytics platform. The company has experienced rapid growth over the past year, doubling its revenue and expanding its customer base to over 2,000 organizations worldwide.
> 
> “We are thrilled to partner with Summit Peak Investments as we enter our next phase of growth,” said Sarah Chen, CEO and Co-Founder of NexaTech Solutions. “This funding will allow us to continue to innovate and deliver on our mission of empowering organizations with the intelligent, intuitive, and scalable solutions they need to transform their data into a competitive advantage.”
> 
> NexaTech’s flagship product, the NexaInsight Platform, leverages artificial intelligence and machine learning to help businesses make faster, smarter decisions. The platform’s unique capabilities, including its natural language query interface and AI-powered predictive analytics, have been a key driver of its success in the market.
> 
> “NexaTech is at the forefront of a massive shift in the business intelligence market,” said David Lee, Managing Partner at Summit Peak Investments. “Their AI-first approach and relentless focus on customer success have positioned them as a clear leader in the space. We are excited to support them as they continue to scale and redefine the future of data analytics.”
> 
> With this new funding, NexaTech plans to expand its presence in Europe and Asia, as well as launch a new research and development center in Berlin, Germany. The company also plans to hire over 200 new employees across all departments in the next year.
